class.description:
A [TextLocalizationCatalog] stores the texts of many keys in many locales (see [LocalizationCatalog] for the layout, the file formats and loading per locale). A key can have a context ([code]"menu"[/code] for the same key in another place), and each locale can have plural forms with its own plural rule.
It replaces a set of [Translation] resources (one per locale and file) with one resource per table. [method to_translations] and [method add_translation] convert between both.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var catalog = TextLocalizationCatalog.new()
catalog.set_text("HELLO", "en", "Hello")
catalog.set_text("HELLO", "de", "Hallo")
catalog.set_text("HELLO", "de", "Hallo!", "menu")
catalog.set_plural_texts("APPLE", "de", ["%d Apfel", "%d Äpfel"])
print(catalog.get_plural_text("APPLE", "de", 3) % 3) # 3 Äpfel
print(catalog.to_text(ResourceTextSerializer.FORMAT_JSON))
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var catalog = new TextLocalizationCatalog();
catalog.SetText("HELLO", "en", "Hello");
catalog.SetText("HELLO", "de", "Hallo");
catalog.SetText("HELLO", "de", "Hallo!", "menu");
catalog.SetPluralTexts("APPLE", "de", ["%d Apfel", "%d Äpfel"]);
GD.Print(catalog.GetPluralText("APPLE", "de", 3)); // %d Äpfel
GD.Print(catalog.ToText(ResourceTextSerializer.Format.Json));
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
